System Design Specification (SDS)
University Ceremony Attire Rental & Marketplace System

Document Version: 1.0

Date: September 2026

System Stack: React 19, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Django 5.x, Django REST Framework (DRF), PostgreSQL, Docker

1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose
The System Design Specification (SDS) defines the complete technical architecture, subsystem designs, database models, frontend component structures, and API contracts for the University Ceremony Attire Rental & Marketplace System. This document serves as the technical blueprint for software engineers, backend developers, UI/UX engineers, and system administrators during implementation and deployment.

1.2 System Overview
The system is a decoupled, three-tier web application designed to connect university students with local apparel designers, boutiques, and formal wear rental vendors.

Presentation Layer: A responsive Single Page Application (SPA) built with React 19, Vite, and Tailwind CSS.

Application Layer: A RESTful API built on Python 3.12, Django 5.x, and Django REST Framework (DRF), managing business logic, role-based authorization, and state transitions.

Database Layer: A PostgreSQL 16 relational database enforcing transactional integrity, relational foreign key constraints, and inventory safety.

Security Layer: Stateless authentication using JSON Web Tokens (JWT) with role-based access control (RBAC).

