2.2 Security Architecture & Authentication Flow
Authentication: Users submit credentials to /api/v1/auth/token/. Upon validation, DRF issues a short-lived access token (60-minute life) and a long-lived refresh token (7-day life).

Authorization Header: The frontend Axios client automatically attaches the header Authorization: Bearer <access_token> to all protected outgoing requests.

Token Refresh: An Axios response interceptor catches 401 Unauthorized responses, requests a new access token via /api/v1/auth/token/refresh/, and retries the failed request seamlessly.

Role-Based Access Control (RBAC): Custom DRF permission classes (IsStudent, IsVerifiedStudent, IsVendor, IsAdmin) validate token claims prior to executing business logic.

